{{ElectionsWV}}
The '''2026 United States Senate election in West Virginia''' will be held on November 3, 2026, to elect a member of the [[United States Senate]] to represent the state of [[West Virginia]]. [[Republican Party (United States)|Republican]] incumbent [[Shelley Moore Capito]] is seeking a third term.<ref>{{Cite web|last=Charles|first=Young|date=December 15, 2025|title=Sen. Shelley Moore Capito announces 2026 reelection bid for U.S. Senate|url=https://www.wvnews.com/news/wvnews/sen-shelley-moore-capito-announces-2026-reelection-bid-for-u-s-senate/article_a470c34e-d03f-4e4e-800d-66c1b7f06310.html|website=West Virginia News}}</ref> She is being challenged by [[Democratic Party (United States)|Democratic]] former [[Morgantown, West Virginia|Morgantown]] councilwoman Rachel Fetty Anderson.

[[Primary elections]] were held on May 12. In the Republican primary, Capito won the nomination with 66.5% of the vote over state senator [[Tom Willis (politician)|Tom Willis]]. Fetty Anderson won the Democratic nomination with 33.2% of the vote over a field of candidates that included former state Senate president [[Jeff Kessler]].

